` "A projection guarded by block? on the same parameter is not a block use: a non-block argument checks clean (eu-oaz72.194)."
h(x): x block? then(x.a, 0)

` "The guard as the condition of if itself: this fixture covers the if form, which then is defined through."
h-if(x): if(x block?, x.a, 0)

` "A negated guard protects the else branch."
h-not(x): x block? not then(0, x.a)

` "and runs its second argument only when the guard holds."
h-and(x): and(x block?, x.a)

` "or runs its second argument only when its first is false: here, when x is a block."
h-or(x): or(x block? not, x.a)

v: h(3)
v-if: h-if(3)
v-not: h-not(3)
v-and: h-and(3)
v-or: h-or(3)
